Now I have a complete understanding of all the coupling points. Let me compile the full implementation plan.

---

## Implementation Plan: Decouple Runner Module from UI Implementation Details

### Problem Statement

The `WorkflowRunner::run_with_ui()` method in `/private/var/folders/_q/qzh8_t6s15388qqf3p6n3d200000gp/T/bench-aosah494/src/runner/workflow.rs` has two concrete coupling points to UI implementation details:

1. **BivvyTheme in Runner** (line 317): The runner constructs `BivvyTheme::new()` and directly calls `theme.format_skipped(...)`, `theme.step_number.apply_to(...)`, `theme.step_title.apply_to(...)`, `theme.dim.apply_to(...)`, and `StatusKind::format(&theme, ...)` to build styled strings, then passes them to `ui.message()`. This means the runner knows about visual styling -- a UI concern.

2. **ProgressBar leak via SpinnerHandle** (line 603): The runner calls `spinner.progress_bar()` which returns `Option<indicatif::ProgressBar>`, then imports and calls `crate::ui::spinner::live_output_callback(bar, ...)` to create an `OutputCallback`. This forces the runner to depend on the `indicatif` crate and on internal spinner implementation details.

### Design Approach

The goal is to make `run_with_ui()` depend only on the `UserInterface` and `SpinnerHandle` trait interfaces, removing any imports of `BivvyTheme`, `live_output_callback`, or `indicatif::ProgressBar` from the runner module.

---

### Part 1: Remove BivvyTheme from Runner

**Strategy**: Add formatting methods to the `UserInterface` trait so the runner can ask the UI to format text instead of doing it directly. The runner will pass semantic data (step number, step name, status kind, reason text) and the UI will return the formatted string.

#### Step 1a: Add formatting methods to `UserInterface` trait

In `/private/var/folders/_q/qzh8_t6s15388qqf3p6n3d200000gp/T/bench-aosah494/src/ui/mod.rs`, add these methods to the `UserInterface` trait with default plain-text implementations:

```rust
/// Format a step header like "[1/7] step_name" or "[1/7] step_name -- title".
/// Returns the formatted string; the caller passes it to `message()` or embeds it in prompts.
fn format_step_header(&self, index: usize, total: usize, name: &str, title: &str) -> String {
    let step_number = format!("[{}/{}]", index + 1, total);
    if name == title {
        format!("{} {}", step_number, name)
    } else {
        format!("{} {} \u{2014} {}", step_number, name, title)
    }
}

/// Format a status message like "Skipped (reason)" or "Blocked (dependency failed)".
/// Returns the formatted string with appropriate icon/styling.
fn format_status(&self, status: StatusKind, message: &str) -> String {
    status.format_plain(message)
}
```

The default implementations use plain text (no colors), which is correct for `MockUI` and as a fallback.

#### Step 1b: Override in `TerminalUI`

In `/private/var/folders/_q/qzh8_t6s15388qqf3p6n3d200000gp/T/bench-aosah494/src/ui/terminal.rs`, add overrides that use `self.theme`:

```rust
fn format_step_header(&self, index: usize, total: usize, name: &str, title: &str) -> String {
    let step_number = format!("[{}/{}]", index + 1, total);
    if name == title {
        format!(
            "{} {}",
            self.theme.step_number.apply_to(&step_number),
            self.theme.step_title.apply_to(name)
